From bcf83dd357975a86212559b1e607f06e95af2ac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yohan <you@example.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:33:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backend: add JSON response mode + safe diagnostics for the
 Gemini AI pipeline

Regenerated cleanly against the current HEAD (feec12e, "Backend: fix ML
loading and add Gemini provider") after the previous patch failed to
apply against a stale base. Confirmed this repo's current
llmClient.ts/aiAssessment.ts/tests/llmClient.test.ts before editing -
no [ai-debug] logging or responseMimeType existed here yet.

CONTEXT / LIMITATION UP FRONT: this sandbox has no network egress to
generativelanguage.googleapis.com, so I could not make a live call with
a real Gemini key and empirically observe which exact failure point is
occurring on your machine. Rather than guess, this change makes two
concrete improvements that address known real failure modes, and adds
safe, targeted diagnostic logging at every stage of the pipeline, so
your next scan (with your real key) will print exactly where it fails.

Confirmed NOT the problem (traced/checked directly, no changes needed):
  - LlmProvider interface unchanged - still exactly
    `complete(request: LlmCompletionRequest): Promise<string>`.
  - llmProviderFromEnv() reads LLM_PROVIDER/LLM_API_KEY/LLM_MODEL fresh
    on every call (inside the scan route handler, not cached at module
    load) - dotenv/import ordering is not a factor.
  - parseLlmSemanticJson() already strips ```json fences before
    parsing.
  - AIAssessment's full field set (phishingIntent, credentialHarvesting,
    financialFraud, impersonation, socialEngineering, attackType,
    summary, recommendedActions, aiContentScore, status) is built
    correctly and never stripped afterward - EmailRecord stores it
    wholesale and the API response spreads the whole record.
  - Batch 5C's separate `recommendations` field is unrelated to and
    unaffected by AIAssessment.recommendedActions.
  - The local ML implementation, risk engine, Batch 5C, Batch 6, and
    frontend are untouched by this change.

Two concrete fixes made (src/services/llmClient.ts):
  1. Added `generationConfig: { responseMimeType: "application/json" }`
     to the Gemini request - targets Gemini replying with prose or a
     format the existing fence-stripping doesn't catch.
  2. On a non-2xx response, now reads and logs (and includes in the
     thrown error) Gemini's own short structured error message (e.g.
     "API key not valid", quota errors, model-not-found) - Google's
     diagnostic text about the request, never email content or the key.

Safe temporary diagnostics added (all console.error, prefixed
"[ai-debug]" for easy grep/removal later):
  - llmProviderFromEnv(): "provider initialized: true/false", provider
    type, and model name (never the API key).
  - createGeminiProvider().complete(): the Gemini HTTP status; on
    failure, Gemini's own error message (bounded, safe); on a
    200-with-no-text response, the finishReason/blockReason enum labels
    (e.g. "SAFETY") - never content.
  - assessAi(): the raw response length and whether it looks like JSON
    (never the text itself); "JSON parse + schema validation: OK" on
    success; on failure, which exact stage failed (provider.complete()
    / JSON.parse() / Zod schema validation / unexpected error) with a
    bounded, content-free detail.

Never logged: API key, email body/content, or the raw LLM response text.

Files changed:
  - src/services/llmClient.ts
  - src/analyzers/aiAssessment.ts
  - tests/llmClient.test.ts (2 new tests added to the existing 9:
    responseMimeType is sent; Gemini's own error message is surfaced
    safely on a non-2xx response)

npm test: 246/246 passing (2 new, 244 baseline unchanged).
npm run build: clean.

How to verify with one fresh .eml scan:
  1. Confirm backend-batch3.5/backend/.env has LLM_PROVIDER=gemini,
     LLM_API_KEY=<your real key>, LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash.
  2. Run the backend so stdout/stderr is visible (npm run dev, or
     npm start after npm run build).
  3. POST a fresh .eml to /api/v1/emails/scan (or use the Scanner UI).
  4. Watch the terminal for lines starting with "[ai-debug]":
       [ai-debug] provider initialized: true | provider: gemini | model: gemini-2.5-flash
       [ai-debug] Gemini HTTP status: <code>
     - If status is not 200: the next line is Gemini's own error
       message (e.g. "API key not valid", "quota exceeded", a 404 for
       an invalid/retired model name) - tells you the exact fix.
     - If status is 200: next you'll see either
       "LLM raw response length: N | starts with '{': true/false" then
       "JSON parse + schema validation: OK" (success), or a line naming
       exactly which stage failed with a bounded reason.
  5. GET /api/v1/emails/:emailId and confirm aiAssessment.status is
     "AVAILABLE" with the full field set populated from a genuine
     model response (not fabricated).
  6. Once confirmed working, the "[ai-debug]" lines can be removed or
     left in place (safe to run anywhere - status codes, boolean
     checks, and Google's own error strings only).
